ile for B, the signed differences would be (2000 - 3000) = -1000 and (2000 - (-3000)) = +5000 → sum = +4000. So the sum of signed differences is +4000 for B, -4000 for A. If 'favorable' means positive, then B has a more favorable sum. Thus, the reason would prefer B. Therefore, the decision reason can be applied: it evaluates pairwise outcome differences and prefers the lottery with a more favorable (positive) sum of differences. The relevant information is the sum of signed differences or absolute differences. In this case, the sum of signed differences favors B. So the reason is applicable and clearly defines a preference (B over A).",
